      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel exhausted and resistant to \"repurposing\" when you have already poured your entire self into your work. Feeling like your main narrative is complete is a valid reflection of a life well-lived. Instead of thinking about finding a \"next big thing,\" could you allow yourself permission simply to rest and exist without the pressure of constant productivity? Giving yourself grace to feel tired is an important part of honoring the immense effort you've already given.",
      "source": "target",
